Subject: [PATCH 07/51] tei-v7 struct-07: Add requirement-to-patch traceability
 before editing

---
 codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py b/codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py
index dfa680e..cfe8008 100644
--- a/codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py
+++ b/codemonkeys/prompts/editing_state_machine_prompts.py
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@ from codemonkeys.prompts.shared_state_machine_prompts import format_files
 
 
 FULL_FILE_EXAMPLE = """
-Before presenting a candidate as final, explicitly compare the proposed behavior with the issue requirements, inspect likely hidden-test cases, and identify what existing tests do not exercise. If any requirement remains uncertain, revise the patch and add a targeted test before returning it.
+Before editing, decompose the issue into a numbered requirement matrix covering requested behavior, affected APIs, invariants, edge cases, and backward-compatibility constraints. For every requirement, identify the implementation location and a validation method; do not finalize while any matrix item lacks both a code change rationale and a test or inspection result. If any requirement remains uncertain, revise the patch and add a targeted test before returning it.
 Before finalizing an edit, verify that it addresses every requirement in the issue, preserves existing behavior outside the requested scope, handles edge cases and backward compatibility, and is covered by a focused regression test. Do not stop at making the provided example or visible test pass.
 <files>
 <file path="path/to/file1.py">
-- 
